        {"q": "What is the difference between sports physiotherapy and general physiotherapy?", "a": "Sports physiotherapy specifically focuses on athletic performance, rapid injury recovery, and preventing future sports-related injuries, often involving higher-level functional agility training compared to general physiotherapy."},
        {"q": "Can you help me recover from a ligament tear?", "a": "Yes, we specialize in rehabilitating acute sports injuries like ACL tears, meniscus injuries, and ankle sprains using evidence-based protocols to safely return you to your sport."},
        {"q": "How soon should I start physiotherapy after a sports injury?", "a": "It is best to seek an assessment within 48 to 72 hours of an acute injury. Early intervention helps control inflammation and prevents scar tissue buildup."},
        {"q": "Do you provide sports massage or kinesiology taping?", "a": "Yes, our sports rehab protocols often include sports massage, myofascial release, and Kinesio taping to support injured muscles and enhance blood flow."},
        {"q": "Can sports physiotherapy improve my athletic performance?", "a": "Absolutely. By addressing biomechanical imbalances, improving joint mobility, and enhancing core stability, we can help optimize your movement efficiency and overall athletic performance."}
