        {"q": "What is chest physiotherapy used for?", "a": "Chest physiotherapy helps clear lung secretions, improve breathing efficiency, and increase oxygenation. It is highly effective for conditions like COPD, asthma, pneumonia, and post-surgical respiratory care."},
        {"q": "Does chest physiotherapy help with chronic cough?", "a": "Yes, techniques like postural drainage, percussion, and vibration help dislodge persistent mucus, making it easier to cough up and clear your airways."},
        {"q": "Can breathing exercises improve asthma symptoms?", "a": "Absolutely. We teach diaphragmatic breathing and pursed-lip breathing techniques that help control shortness of breath and improve overall lung capacity for asthma patients."},
        {"q": "Is chest physiotherapy safe for elderly patients?", "a": "Yes, it is extremely safe and highly recommended for elderly patients, especially those bedridden or recovering from chest infections, to prevent severe respiratory complications."},
        {"q": "How often should I do breathing exercises?", "a": "Depending on your condition, your physiotherapist will design a daily regimen. Often, practicing prescribed breathing exercises 2 to 3 times a day yields the best pulmonary results."}
