        {"q": "How many physiotherapy sessions are needed for knee osteoarthritis?", "a": "While you may feel relief in 3-4 sessions, a structured program of 8-12 sessions over a few months is usually required to build sufficient muscle strength to unload the arthritic joint."},
        {"q": "Can physiotherapy provide immediate knee pain relief?", "a": "Yes, techniques like manual therapy, taping, and electrotherapy (like TENS) can provide significant short-term pain relief immediately after a session."},
        {"q": "How long does meniscus tear recovery take with physio?", "a": "A mild to moderate meniscus tear managed conservatively with physiotherapy typically takes 4 to 8 weeks to heal sufficiently for normal daily activities."},
        {"q": "Will my knee pain come back after I stop physiotherapy?", "a": "If you maintain the home exercise program and lifestyle modifications prescribed by your physiotherapist, the risk of your knee pain returning is significantly reduced."},
        {"q": "How do I know if my knee physiotherapy is working?", "a": "Signs of progress include decreased pain, reduced morning stiffness, improved ability to walk or climb stairs, and an overall increase in your knee's range of motion."}
